\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. A safe stronghold our God is still,
\par A trusty shield and weapon;
\par He'll help us clear from all the ill
\par That hath us now 
\par o'ertaken.
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par The ancient prince of hell 
\par Hath risen with purpose fell;
\par Strong mail of craft and power 
\par He weareth in this hour;
\par On earth is not his fellow.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. With force of arms we nothing can, 
\par Full soon were we down-ridden;
\par But for us fights the proper Man,
\par Whom God Himself hath bidden.
\par Ask ye: Who is this same?
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par Christ Jesus is His name,
\par The Lord Sabaoth's Son;
\par He, and no other one,
\par Shall conquer in the battle.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. And were this world all devils o'er,
\par And watching to devour us,
\par We lay it not to heart so 
\par sore;
\par Not they can overpower us.
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par And let the prince of ill
\par Look grim as e'er he will,
\par He harms us not a whit:
\par For why? His doom is writ;
\par A word shall quickly slay him.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. God's word, for all their 
\par craft and force
\par One moment will not linger,
\par But, spite of hell, shall have its couse;
\par 'Tis written by His finger.
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par And though they take our life,
\par Goods, honour, children, wife,
\par Yet is their profit small:
\par These things shall vanish all;
\par The city of God remaineth.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b 
\par }

